  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of livelihoods,WASH and protection support vulnerable people in Sahar.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project envisages providing integrated livelihoods, Water Sanitation and hygiene (WASH) and Protection support to the most vulnerable and at -risk Internal displacement peoples (IDPs) and host communities of Alshatt, Mahlah, Al -Qasasbah, Ban Aweer Al -Gharbi and Bani Moath in Sahar district of Sa&apos;adah governorate, which has been identified based on the prevailing gaps in food security and agriculture, Protection, and Water Sanitation and hygiene (WASH) needs gaps. The project design has been informed by the recent June 2023 rapid need assessment, ongoing programmatic experience, and consultations with local stakeholders, including the food security and agriculture Cluster (FSAC), Water Sanitation and hygiene (WASH) and protection clusters. Oxfam intends to reach 21,805 people (6484  women, 4779  girls, 4399  boys, 6143  men) and has strongly embedded gender equality, protection, safeguarding, and do -no -harm approaches to ensure the provision of assistance in a safe and dignified manner. The project employs a vulnerability -based targeting criterion by targeting Households (HHs) and individuals who suffer from malnutrition, and other forms of vulnerability such as female -headed households, elderly, persons with disabilities and chronic illness, Households (HHs) with more children and unable to meet their food consumption needs, and those expose to protection risks, and lack access to Water Sanitation and hygiene (WASH) services. The project has three integrated components/outcomes. The food security and livelihoods component (outcome 1) will build the resilience of the most vulnerable Households (HHs) of the project aims by providing temporary employment opportunities through rehabilitating community infrastructure using the Cash for Work (CFW) modality (15 -days/month for 3 months) and the participating households will receive YER 67,934.78  equals to USD 125/ per month, enabling them to cover 90 -95 % of the minimum food basket (output 1). Micro -businesses support c</narrative>
  </description>
